# Deane Auto Repairs — go-live reminders

When the user mentions domain pointing, DNS, custom domain, hosting, GitHub Pages custom domain, go-live, or making the website public:

## SEO / domain launch checklist
Remind them and offer to do this pass together:

1. Update Structured Data / JSON-LD URLs from GitHub Pages to the live domain
2. Add `canonical` link to the live domain
3. Add `robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml`
4. Add Open Graph / social share meta (title, description, image)
5. Submit the live domain + sitemap in Google Search Console (and Bing if useful)
6. **Google Business Profile (Google Maps)**
   - Status as of **31 Aug 2026**: registered, **still waiting for verification** (user confirmed)
   - When user says verified (or around **~7 Sep 2026** if still silent): help with post-verify steps below; do not nag daily while waiting
   - If verified, help with:
     - Website URL = live domain (e.g. `https://www.deaneauto.co.nz`)
     - Confirm phone `0800 625 9827`, hours Mon–Sat 8:30am–5:30pm / Sunday closed
     - Replace site “Open in Google Maps” with the official GBP Maps link
     - Suggest uploading workshop / storefront photos
   - If still pending: ask which verification method they’re using and wait; do not nag daily
7. Confirm Google Business Profile website URL matches the live domain once claimed

## Report / admin launch checklist (same pass)
Also remind:

1. Host admin + customer report links on a stable public URL
2. Fix mobile login / photo upload from phone
3. Switch booking/report email to SMTP (not mailto-only)
4. Do remaining report/admin polish in the same deployment pass

Do not overbuild; confirm requirements first for larger features.
Do not push private “password wall” as a substitute for proper go-live unless the user asks.

## Render instance (current choice)
On 18 Aug 2026 the shop chose **Render Free** to test deploy only.

When they say the website is **正式上线**, going live, sending real customer quotes, or pointing `www.deaneauto.co.nz` for public use: **remind them to switch the Web Service from Free to Starter** and attach a persistent disk at `/data` (DATA_DIR=/data, UPLOADS_DIR=/data/uploads). Free sleeps and cannot keep quotes/reports/photos.

Do not nag while they are still testing Free.

## After Render is running (future architecture)
The shop chose **Render first** so customers can open quote links and Accept on their phones.

When the user says Render is live, quotes/reports work on a phone, or asks about hosting cost / moving off Render / serverless: remind them (once, briefly) to consider later:

- **Cloudflare Pages** — public website
- **Cloudflare Workers** (serverless) — quote Accept / report / admin APIs
- **Supabase** — database + photo storage

This is a rewrite, not a hosting switch. Do not start it unless they ask. Do not push it during the current Render setup.

